        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "daebdb77-4806-5985-9556-e6a4b18950ae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Heinrich Marschner, Carl Maria von Weber\n- Products: Der Templer und die Jüdin\n- Topics: German opera, Romantic music\n\nFacts:\n- Carl Maria von Weber was born on 18 or 19 November 1786 and died on 5 June 1826.\n- Carl Maria von Weber was a German composer, conductor, pianist, guitarist, and critic, and he was one of the first significant composers of the Romantic school.\n- Heinrich Marschner was born on 16 August 1795 and died on 14 December 1861.\n- Heinrich Marschner was regarded as the most important composer of German opera between Weber and Wagner.\n- Der Templer und die Jüdin is a three-act opera by Heinrich Marschner.\n- Der Templer und die Jüdin was designated as a grosse romantische Oper and its title translates as \"The Templar and the Jewess.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
